(boom reverberates)

00:00:03.274 --> 00:00:04.160
- Hello, Believe Nation.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.337
Today I'm going to talk
about the seven ways

00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:09.314
to start your perfect day.

00:00:09.314 --> 00:00:10.960
♫ Nine

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.158
♫ Eight

00:00:12.158 --> 00:00:12.991
♫ Seven

00:00:12.991 --> 00:00:15.305
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:15.305 --> 00:00:17.081
♫ Seven

00:00:17.081 --> 00:00:18.767
- So I'm big believer in morning routines.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.972
I think that if you
start your day off right,

00:00:20.972 --> 00:00:23.215
it carries through to
the rest of your day.

00:00:23.215 --> 00:00:25.552
But if you start your
day off wrong, negative,

00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:26.736
missing your first thing,

00:00:26.736 --> 00:00:28.209
whatever that first habit
is you're supposed to do,

00:00:28.209 --> 00:00:29.268
if you miss that,

00:00:29.268 --> 00:00:31.133
then you're likely to
cheat on the rest of it.

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:33.099
Right, like if you say
you're going to eat healthy,

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.229
and then you start by going to get

00:00:34.229 --> 00:00:36.688
that really junky Starbucks
drink in the morning,

00:00:36.688 --> 00:00:39.216
you're unlikely to be
healthy the rest of the day.

00:00:39.216 --> 00:00:40.097
You're unlikely to follow through

00:00:40.097 --> 00:00:41.967
on all the other goals you
said you were going to do.

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:44.764
So why it's so important
to have a morning routine

00:00:44.764 --> 00:00:46.342
that sets you up for success.

00:00:46.342 --> 00:00:49.127
This is probably the
topic of my next book,

00:00:49.127 --> 00:00:50.441
or at least a good chunk of it.

00:00:50.441 --> 00:00:53.516
I find a lot of people, once
they find their one word,

00:00:53.516 --> 00:00:55.359
it's super helpful, it's really powerful.

00:00:55.359 --> 00:00:56.192
But how do you make sure

00:00:56.192 --> 00:00:59.855
that you live your one
word every single day?

00:00:59.855 --> 00:01:02.659
And it comes from starting up
with a great morning routine.

00:01:02.659 --> 00:01:03.955
Now these are seven strategies

00:01:03.955 --> 00:01:05.239
I'm going to share with you today.

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:06.072
You don't necessarily have to

00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:07.532
apply all of them to your life.

00:01:07.532 --> 00:01:10.516
What I encourage you to do is
test one at a time for a week.

00:01:10.516 --> 00:01:11.819
Just test adding this one thing

00:01:11.819 --> 00:01:13.571
to your morning routine for the week.

00:01:13.571 --> 00:01:14.529
And see, do you feel better?

00:01:14.529 --> 00:01:15.386
Do you have more energy?

00:01:15.386 --> 00:01:16.736
Was it a waste of time?

00:01:16.736 --> 00:01:18.937
All you've lost is a few minutes

00:01:18.937 --> 00:01:20.314
every day for one week, right?

00:01:20.314 --> 00:01:21.852
But the upside is tremendous.

00:01:21.852 --> 00:01:23.021
So test each one out,

00:01:23.021 --> 00:01:25.015
and let me know which
one works best for you.

00:01:25.015 --> 00:01:28.400
(hip hop music)

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.938
So the first way to start your
perfect day off is to get up.

00:01:31.938 --> 00:01:34.616
Get rid of the snooze button.

00:01:34.616 --> 00:01:37.026
Now while some of you may be
throwing tomatoes at me now,

00:01:37.026 --> 00:01:39.955
or clicking away, you're
addicted to that snooze button.

00:01:39.955 --> 00:01:41.252
Let's talk about some of the reasons why

00:01:41.252 --> 00:01:42.568
you shouldn't be snoozing.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.164
First off, science has proven
it's actually bad for you.

00:01:45.164 --> 00:01:46.646
You actually feel a lot more groggy.

00:01:46.646 --> 00:01:49.321
If you just hear the
alarm, and you get up,

00:01:49.321 --> 00:01:52.006
you're much more likely to
have an energized morning.

00:01:52.006 --> 00:01:54.275
Where if you snooze, and then you snooze,

00:01:54.275 --> 00:01:55.915
your brain falls back asleep,

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.406
and then gets up, and then falls asleep,

00:01:57.406 --> 00:01:58.676
and then gets back up again.

00:01:58.676 --> 00:02:00.931
And while that may feel
good in the short term,

00:02:00.931 --> 00:02:03.353
you're going to have a
couple hours of grogginess

00:02:03.353 --> 00:02:05.234
that will not help you.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:06.579
The other thing is on
a subconscious level,

00:02:06.579 --> 00:02:08.941
you're training yourself to fail.

00:02:08.941 --> 00:02:10.876
You're training yourself to say,

00:02:10.876 --> 00:02:14.409
this is a goal that I had,
and I didn't do it, right?

00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:17.810
My goal is to wake up at this
time, and I didn't do it.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.084
I'm snoozing, I didn't do it.

00:02:19.084 --> 00:02:20.897
I snooze again, I didn't do it again.

00:02:20.897 --> 00:02:23.256
You're training yourself that it's okay

00:02:23.256 --> 00:02:26.113
to set a goal for yourself for a new habit

00:02:26.113 --> 00:02:27.550
and not follow through.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:30.167
And this is how you're
starting every single day.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:32.385
You're starting the
day by saying it's okay

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:35.147
to let myself down and
disappoint myself again.

00:02:35.147 --> 00:02:37.192
That is not a powerful
way to start your day.

00:02:37.192 --> 00:02:40.349
So that, combined with
the science, get up.

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:42.395
Put your clock somewhere
else across the room.

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:44.746
Whatever strategy you want
to use, it doesn't matter,

00:02:44.746 --> 00:02:48.200
stop pressing the snooze
button, and just get up.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.867
(hip hop music)

00:02:51.842 --> 00:02:53.849
Number two, drink some water.

00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:55.075
Your body is 60% water.

00:02:55.075 --> 00:02:57.113
Your brain is 75% water.

00:02:57.113 --> 00:02:59.527
One of the main reasons
why you're so tired

00:02:59.527 --> 00:03:01.292
in the morning is you're dehydrated.

00:03:01.292 --> 00:03:03.647
You've sweat a lot of water out overnight.

00:03:03.647 --> 00:03:05.313
You've just been sleeping for five, six,

00:03:05.313 --> 00:03:09.019
seven, eight, nine hours
without any hydration.

00:03:09.019 --> 00:03:11.572
You need to get up and
not reach for coffee,

00:03:11.572 --> 00:03:13.521
but reach for a glass of water.

00:03:13.521 --> 00:03:15.462
It will make you feel better.

00:03:15.462 --> 00:03:16.603
The science has proved it.

00:03:16.603 --> 00:03:18.121
It's one of the most consistent things

00:03:18.121 --> 00:03:20.848
that I think really
everybody should be doing

00:03:20.848 --> 00:03:23.216
to give themselves more
energy in the morning.

00:03:23.216 --> 00:03:25.522
On top of having more energy
and feeling less tired,

00:03:25.522 --> 00:03:27.455
drinking water will help you lose weight,

00:03:27.455 --> 00:03:29.785
and will help you fight
off sicknesses as well.

00:03:29.785 --> 00:03:31.529
And as a special bonus, I'd say,

00:03:31.529 --> 00:03:34.039
try adding some lemon to your water, too.

00:03:34.039 --> 00:03:35.702
Adding some lemon to
your water in the morning

00:03:35.702 --> 00:03:38.269
will give you vitamin C to
help boost your immune system,

00:03:38.269 --> 00:03:39.712
will allow you to have better skin,

00:03:39.712 --> 00:03:41.683
and will fight bad breath as well.

00:03:41.683 --> 00:03:44.161
A good tip is if you're under 150 pounds,

00:03:44.161 --> 00:03:46.010
add half a lemon to your water,

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.478
and if you're over 150 pounds,

00:03:47.478 --> 00:03:49.646
add the full lemon into your water.

00:03:49.646 --> 00:03:50.776
It makes a difference.

00:03:50.776 --> 00:03:54.131
Stop reaching for coffee,
reach for water first.

00:03:54.131 --> 00:03:56.798
(hip hop music)

00:03:57.719 --> 00:03:59.250
Number three is music.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.591
Music is so, so, so, so important,

00:04:01.591 --> 00:04:03.048
because it changes your state.

00:04:03.048 --> 00:04:07.556
When a good song comes on
that makes you want to bounce,

00:04:07.556 --> 00:04:09.318
it instantly lifts your mood.

00:04:09.318 --> 00:04:11.317
It instantly gives you more energy.

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.304
And so I have a Believe playlist,

00:04:13.304 --> 00:04:15.680
and one of the things that
I do is every morning,

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:18.307
I wake up, and with my
wife, we put on a dance song

00:04:18.307 --> 00:04:20.713
that we both enjoy, and
we dance, and we groove,

00:04:20.713 --> 00:04:21.603
and we dance with each other.

00:04:21.603 --> 00:04:23.250
It's a good time to bond,

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.738
but also to get us
shakin', to give us energy.

00:04:25.738 --> 00:04:28.753
And so I would encourage you
to make your own playlist.

00:04:28.753 --> 00:04:30.733
Think about songs that
make you want to move,

00:04:30.733 --> 00:04:32.425
that make you just, when it comes on,

00:04:32.425 --> 00:04:35.025
you have to bounce, you
have to get excited.

00:04:35.025 --> 00:04:35.965
And start your day with that,

00:04:35.965 --> 00:04:37.916
so that you have energy in the morning

00:04:37.916 --> 00:04:39.425
after drinking your glass of water,

00:04:39.425 --> 00:04:41.253
and you're ready to take on the day.

00:04:41.253 --> 00:04:44.541
(hip hop music)

00:04:44.541 --> 00:04:46.256
Number four is gratitude.

00:04:46.256 --> 00:04:48.255
It's impossible to be
grateful for something,

00:04:48.255 --> 00:04:51.893
and really sad, and depressed,
and angry at the same time.

00:04:51.893 --> 00:04:53.498
And so I find it really helpful

00:04:53.498 --> 00:04:55.605
to have a quick morning gratitude session

00:04:55.605 --> 00:04:56.662
just to think about three things

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:58.250
that I'm grateful for, for the day.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.585
And so it's something I do with my wife.

00:05:00.585 --> 00:05:03.516
We'll wake up, we'll
grab a glass of water,

00:05:03.516 --> 00:05:05.066
we'll then dance to a song,

00:05:05.066 --> 00:05:06.659
and then we'll sit down for four minutes,

00:05:06.659 --> 00:05:07.647
another song will come on,

00:05:07.647 --> 00:05:10.262
it's calming, peaceful,
relaxing, no lyrics,

00:05:10.262 --> 00:05:12.316
and we'll just put our
hand over our heart,

00:05:12.316 --> 00:05:14.430
and think of three things
that we're grateful for,

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:15.805
for that day.

00:05:15.805 --> 00:05:17.816
And I think that really helps set us up,

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:21.193
just the awareness, the
shifting of perspective,

00:05:21.193 --> 00:05:22.749
the not complaining about the things

00:05:22.749 --> 00:05:23.927
that are outside our control,

00:05:23.927 --> 00:05:26.026
and just recognizing that we
have a lot of amazing things

00:05:26.026 --> 00:05:27.618
that we have in our lives,

00:05:27.618 --> 00:05:30.110
and not only focusing on the
things that we don't have.

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:32.650
For my view, it's not just
recognizing what's great,

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.090
it's also the frustration
that you want more, right?

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.906
Like I am equally happy with what I have,

00:05:36.906 --> 00:05:39.089
I'm so grateful for it, and I want more.

00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:40.528
I want to go out and have a bigger impact.

00:05:40.528 --> 00:05:42.156
What I've done is not enough.

00:05:42.156 --> 00:05:43.947
I don't want to just
rest on what's happened.

00:05:43.947 --> 00:05:45.401
But if you only focus on this part

00:05:45.401 --> 00:05:47.288
of wanting more, wanting
more, wanting more,

00:05:47.288 --> 00:05:49.485
and not focusing on what you already have

00:05:49.485 --> 00:05:52.196
and how great life is, then
you're never going to be happy.

00:05:52.196 --> 00:05:53.442
And so I find that that combination

00:05:53.442 --> 00:05:54.942
is really, really helpful.

00:05:54.942 --> 00:05:57.609
(hip hop music)

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.573
Number five is review
your goals for the day.

00:06:00.573 --> 00:06:02.879
I find it really helpful
to have a plan for the day.

00:06:02.879 --> 00:06:04.443
And if you look at successful people,

00:06:04.443 --> 00:06:05.644
they often have a plan.

00:06:05.644 --> 00:06:06.966
They know their outcome for what they want

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.488
to accomplish for the day.

00:06:08.488 --> 00:06:10.776
Again, if you don't have a plan,

00:06:10.776 --> 00:06:12.540
you can guarantee that
everybody else around you

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.984
has a plan for you, right?

00:06:13.984 --> 00:06:15.562
People have a plan for you.

00:06:15.562 --> 00:06:16.651
If you open up your email,

00:06:16.651 --> 00:06:19.664
there's a whole bunch of
people who have a plan for you,

00:06:19.664 --> 00:06:22.062
and a plan for your time,

00:06:22.062 --> 00:06:23.594
where you need to fight for that time,

00:06:23.594 --> 00:06:25.613
you need to fight for what you want to do.

00:06:25.613 --> 00:06:27.238
And so reviewing your
goals and remembering,

00:06:27.238 --> 00:06:28.753
what am I trying to do today?

00:06:28.753 --> 00:06:29.817
What's my outcome today?

00:06:29.817 --> 00:06:31.538
What do I want to accomplish today?

00:06:31.538 --> 00:06:34.498
And start setting up
walls for yourself to say,

00:06:34.498 --> 00:06:37.545
nobody is going to crush
through these chunks of time,

00:06:37.545 --> 00:06:40.783
because this is what I
want to get done today.

00:06:40.783 --> 00:06:42.374
And so reviewing that in the morning,

00:06:42.374 --> 00:06:45.032
reviewing that consistently,
reviewing that every day,

00:06:45.032 --> 00:06:46.859
allows you to have a more powerful day

00:06:46.859 --> 00:06:49.065
where you're more likely to
follow through on your goals.

00:06:49.065 --> 00:06:50.788
If you can't remember what your goals are,

00:06:50.788 --> 00:06:52.955
you're probably not going to
get them accomplished today.

00:06:52.955 --> 00:06:55.622
(hip hop music)

00:06:56.529 --> 00:06:58.058
Number six is exercise.

00:06:58.058 --> 00:07:00.153
This is another way to
change your state, right?

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.906
If you're sleepy, and you're like this,

00:07:01.906 --> 00:07:03.806
and you're complaining,

00:07:03.806 --> 00:07:06.071
you're probably not going
to feel really powerful.

00:07:06.071 --> 00:07:07.877
But if you get up, you drink some water,

00:07:07.877 --> 00:07:10.144
you put on some music,
you do a quick exercise,

00:07:10.144 --> 00:07:12.111
you do jumping jacks, you do some pushups.

00:07:12.111 --> 00:07:14.990
For me I take my dog, Teemo, for a walk.

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.682
He's sittin' out here,
that's why I pointed.

00:07:16.682 --> 00:07:18.681
You can't see him on
camera, but he's out here.

00:07:18.681 --> 00:07:20.165
That's why I pointed to him.

00:07:20.165 --> 00:07:22.695
Getting some kind of
exercise in the morning

00:07:22.695 --> 00:07:25.128
gets your body movin',
gets the blood pumping,

00:07:25.128 --> 00:07:26.362
gets things flowing,

00:07:26.362 --> 00:07:29.238
even if it's 30 seconds of
jumping jacks, just something.

00:07:29.238 --> 00:07:32.915
At the end of our walk, we'll
run up 13 flights of stairs,

00:07:32.915 --> 00:07:34.649
and we'll both be panting and tired,

00:07:34.649 --> 00:07:38.778
but I feel great, energized,
and ready to take on the day.

00:07:38.778 --> 00:07:41.103
So adding some form of physical activity,

00:07:41.103 --> 00:07:42.820
doesn't have to be half an hour walk,

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.458
could be 30 seconds of jumping jacks

00:07:44.458 --> 00:07:47.226
at a high intensity just
to get the blood flowing,

00:07:47.226 --> 00:07:49.050
will make a difference
to your energy level.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:52.286
(hip hop music)

00:07:52.286 --> 00:07:54.589
And number seven is be inspired.

00:07:54.589 --> 00:07:55.422
It's really important.

00:07:55.422 --> 00:07:56.684
I've talked about this a lot in my videos

00:07:56.684 --> 00:07:58.833
to have an environment for success.

00:07:58.833 --> 00:08:01.200
That whenever you felt
energized, excited, motivated,

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.453
bold, empowered, want to do great things,

00:08:03.453 --> 00:08:04.661
what was it that caused that,

00:08:04.661 --> 00:08:06.982
and put that into your daily routine?

00:08:06.982 --> 00:08:08.656
So you have your goals, right?

00:08:08.656 --> 00:08:10.697
We have your list of goals
that you want to accomplish,

00:08:10.697 --> 00:08:11.530
you're reading those through,

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.651
but there's still that voice
in your head that will say,

00:08:13.651 --> 00:08:14.723
you can't do that.

00:08:14.723 --> 00:08:16.477
Who are you to think that
that's going to happen, right?

00:08:16.477 --> 00:08:18.536
That's never going to happen for you.

00:08:18.536 --> 00:08:22.534
You need the voice to say, I'm
going to crush these things.

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:24.006
Remember who you are.

00:08:24.006 --> 00:08:25.196
These things are powerful.

00:08:25.196 --> 00:08:26.566
You're going to go and kill it.

00:08:26.566 --> 00:08:28.300
You can do this.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.706
And so if it's watching a video,
or listening to a podcast,

00:08:30.706 --> 00:08:32.765
or reading a book, or whatever it is,

00:08:32.765 --> 00:08:34.362
however long it takes
you to get in that state

00:08:34.362 --> 00:08:36.823
of feeling powerful, and unstoppable,

00:08:36.823 --> 00:08:38.124
you want to do that daily.

00:08:38.124 --> 00:08:40.455
So why I have the Entspresso
series in the morning,

00:08:40.455 --> 00:08:43.025
as a video series to
help me get energized,

00:08:43.025 --> 00:08:46.510
to be hanging around a
successful person for 10 minutes,

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.395
to give me a boost,

00:08:48.395 --> 00:08:50.403
to not just give me a
strategy for what I can do,

00:08:50.403 --> 00:08:52.404
but also just the motivation.

00:08:52.404 --> 00:08:54.638
When you are around
other successful people,

00:08:54.638 --> 00:08:57.090
you instantly become more successful.

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.602
When you're around hardworking people,

00:08:58.602 --> 00:09:00.664
you instantly want to
start working harder.

00:09:00.664 --> 00:09:04.420
If you're around lazy,
slow, apathetic people,

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:05.253
it's really hard.

00:09:05.253 --> 00:09:07.752
You're going to become
lazy, slow, and apathetic,

00:09:07.752 --> 00:09:09.451
where you know you have a higher gear,

00:09:09.451 --> 00:09:11.149
you know you could play stronger,

00:09:11.149 --> 00:09:14.362
you know you can go faster,
you know you can get up there.

00:09:14.362 --> 00:09:15.753
So you need to design that environment.

00:09:15.753 --> 00:09:17.723
You need to design that
into your morning routine,

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:19.417
so that you're living it daily.

00:09:19.417 --> 00:09:22.315
So those are my seven ways on
how to start the perfect day.

00:09:22.315 --> 00:09:23.653
I'd love to know, what did you think?

00:09:23.653 --> 00:09:24.941
What did you learn from this video?

00:09:24.941 --> 00:09:26.626
Which one was your favorite way?

